# Deep Research Request: Complete History of 44 Mill Street, Westwood, MA

## Primary Research Objective
Compile a comprehensive history of the property known by multiple identifiers:
- 44 Mill Street, Westwood, MA
- 0 Mill Street, Westwood, MA  
- Assessor's Map 28, Lot 014
- 1974 Restricted Wetland Area #44

Focus on documenting all boundary changes, development attempts, ownership transitions, and the evolution of environmental restrictions affecting this parcel.

## Critical Background Context
This property has been subject to "dozens of development applications" over the past 50 years but finding consolidated records has proven extremely difficult. The property is subject to a permanent wetland restriction deed recorded on April 24, 1974, under Massachusetts G.L. c.131 §40A, identifying it as Wetland Area #44. The 1974 record lists Joseph F. Hearne and Myra R. Hearne as owners.

## Specific Research Requirements

### 1. Chain of Title & Ownership History
- Start with Joseph F. and Myra R. Hearne (owners as of 1974)
- Trace forward to current owner(s)
- Trace backward to original land grants/subdivision
- Identify all ownership transfers with dates and deed references
- Note any estates, trusts, or corporate owners
- Find any foreclosures, tax takings, or disputed ownership

### 2. Property Boundary Evolution
- Document all recorded surveys showing this parcel
- Identify every instance where lot lines changed
- Find any lot splits, combinations, or reconfigurations
- Locate ANR (Approval Not Required) plans that may have adjusted boundaries
- Track changes in lot size (square footage/acreage) over time
- Identify any boundary disputes or encroachment issues

